WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.237
This retention query starts from the recent-activity view.

00:00:03.237 --> 00:00:06.807
A CTE finds the last transaction per customer.

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:10.877
Another CTE applies a sixty-day inactivity threshold.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:14.227
That threshold is intentionally report-specific.

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.707
If another report wants ninety days, the shared activity view does not need to change.

00:00:19.707 --> 00:00:25.932
Connect this idea to a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:31.067
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:38.057
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.057 --> 00:00:43.467
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:48.560
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
